WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.668 line:0%
-Unfortunately for you,
you also confess

00:00:02.668 --> 00:00:04.837 line:0%
to the crime of fraud...

00:00:04.837 --> 00:00:06.940 line:0%
to being a charlatan...

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:10.009 line:0%
a purveyor of lies
and narcotics.

00:00:11.277 --> 00:00:15.248 line:0%
You're an animal who preys
on the despair of the poor...

00:00:15.248 --> 00:00:16.883 line:0%
and who abuses
their trust in you

00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:18.685 line:0%
for your own ill-gotten gains.

00:00:18.685 --> 00:00:22.589 line:0%
You are confessing
to those crimes, are you not?

00:00:22.589 --> 00:00:24.123
-Well, damn.

00:00:24.123 --> 00:00:26.759
When you put it like that...
[ Laughter ]

00:00:26.759 --> 00:00:28.828
-Welcome back.
We're here with James McAvoy!

00:00:28.828 --> 00:00:30.029
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:30.029 --> 00:00:32.565
That was a clip
from "The Book of Clarence."

00:00:32.565 --> 00:00:37.504
This looks like a grand-scale
biblical epic.

00:00:37.504 --> 00:00:39.371
-You've got a biblical epic
on your hands.

00:00:39.371 --> 00:00:40.540
-But it's also very funny.

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:42.474
It's sort of a comedic
biblical epic.

00:00:42.474 --> 00:00:45.311
-It is funny.
It's heartfelt. It's full of...

00:00:45.311 --> 00:00:48.180
It's, dare I say it,
it's full of faith.

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:51.951
Um, and it is just wild.

00:00:51.951 --> 00:00:54.687
That director, Jeymes Samuel,
man, he is special.

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:55.855
He's something different.

00:00:55.855 --> 00:00:58.424
-You are playing
Pontius Pilate in this role.

00:00:58.424 --> 00:00:59.725
You are --
You were raised Catholic.

00:00:59.725 --> 00:01:01.394
Is this a character
that you put a lot of thought

00:01:01.394 --> 00:01:02.695
into over the years?
-Finally,

00:01:02.695 --> 00:01:05.264
they've let me play a Catholic.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.264 --> 00:01:07.500
All I wanted to do
was play a Catholic.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:08.968
[ Laughter ]

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:10.870
But after the actions
of the Catholic Church

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:12.605
in the last few years,
it wasn't fashionable.

00:01:12.605 --> 00:01:14.541
Um...
[ Laughter ]

00:01:14.541 --> 00:01:16.175
Thank you for --

00:01:16.175 --> 00:01:20.312
Thank you for this secondary
roll-over laugh.

00:01:20.312 --> 00:01:22.181
Those four people...

00:01:22.181 --> 00:01:24.017
-It's also
their first show of 2024.

00:01:24.017 --> 00:01:25.884
It's like everybody's
getting back into shape.

00:01:25.884 --> 00:01:27.887
-You guys don't
get invited back.

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:32.124
Um, yeah. You're in trouble now.
I'm not. I hope.

00:01:32.124 --> 00:01:34.994
Um, yeah,
I was brought up a Catholic.

00:01:34.994 --> 00:01:36.429
Was it fun to play a Catholic?
Yeah, it was great.

00:01:36.429 --> 00:01:37.864
And, no, I didn't
play a Catholic,

00:01:37.864 --> 00:01:41.000
but I was in a biblical epic.
-And you got to wear, uh...

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:42.935
You made a choice.

00:01:42.935 --> 00:01:44.270
You made a choice
for Pontius Pilate,

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:47.139
which we saw in the clip,
which was guyliner.

00:01:47.139 --> 00:01:48.574
-Yeah.
-Yeah, a very heavily

00:01:48.574 --> 00:01:51.944
eyelined Pontius Pilate.
-Yeah.

00:01:51.944 --> 00:01:55.681
So, he's -- he's kind of
like -- He used to be a soldier.

00:01:55.681 --> 00:01:58.351
Now he's a bureaucrat, right?
That's what I felt about him.

00:01:58.351 --> 00:01:59.919
And I thought,
"How do I make it look

00:01:59.919 --> 00:02:01.820
like he would rather be
anywhere else?"

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:05.290
And I was like, "Guyliner."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:05.290 --> 00:02:06.325
Honestly,
because I was thinking,

00:02:06.325 --> 00:02:09.061
like, the Romans,
they were kind of...

00:02:09.061 --> 00:02:11.297
they were kind of experimental.
-Yeah.

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:12.465
They were having
a grand old time.

00:02:12.465 --> 00:02:14.300
They were having a grand
old time -- orgies --

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:16.369
[ Laughter ]
...and I was like --

00:02:16.369 --> 00:02:18.838
-First footing in Rome...
-First footing.

00:02:18.838 --> 00:02:21.774
-...totally different.
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:21.774 --> 00:02:24.243
-First footing in a toga,
it can get messy.

00:02:24.243 --> 00:02:28.381
Um, and I was just thinking
that maybe if I've got guyliner,

00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:30.616
it would just look like
I'd rather be in an orgy

00:02:30.616 --> 00:02:32.718
than dealing with a messiah.
-Yeah.

00:02:32.718 --> 00:02:35.588
And so LaKeith Stanfield, uh,
he is someone who has

00:02:35.588 --> 00:02:37.923
sort of noticed how much
attention Jesus is getting.

00:02:37.923 --> 00:02:38.858
-Yeah.
-Basically, he's trying

00:02:38.858 --> 00:02:40.726
to be another messiah.
-Yeah.

00:02:40.726 --> 00:02:42.695
He looks at Jesus as a guy
who's on the make.

00:02:42.695 --> 00:02:44.630
He doesn't believe,
he has no faith,

00:02:44.630 --> 00:02:46.199
and he doesn't believe in God.

00:02:46.199 --> 00:02:50.269
So he's like, "This guy is doing
great with a scheme.

00:02:50.269 --> 00:02:52.205
So I'm going to -- I want to be
like that in five years.

00:02:52.205 --> 00:02:53.506
I want to be like that now."

00:02:53.506 --> 00:02:56.475
So he's like, "I'm gonna
just do what Jesus is doing."

00:02:56.475 --> 00:02:58.544
So all the stuff that happens
to Jesus happens to him.

00:02:58.544 --> 00:03:00.947
LaKeith is brilliant
in this film.

00:03:00.947 --> 00:03:02.582
He is an amazing actor,
and he's so good.

00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:04.717
-He is a really --
He's a really wonderful actor

00:03:04.717 --> 00:03:07.419
and it is such a fun idea
for a film.

00:03:07.419 --> 00:03:09.122
And you --
Is it true that you did

00:03:09.122 --> 00:03:10.656
consider life in the clergy

00:03:10.656 --> 00:03:12.424
before you found
your way to this?

00:03:12.424 --> 00:03:13.992
-Yeah.
Look, I really wanted to travel,

00:03:13.992 --> 00:03:17.864
and I did consider, um,
becoming a missionary.

00:03:17.864 --> 00:03:20.566
And then I also realized
that I would have to be celibate

00:03:20.566 --> 00:03:22.535
if I became a priest,

00:03:22.535 --> 00:03:25.304
and I was just starting to get
luck with the opposite sex,

00:03:25.304 --> 00:03:26.805
and I thought,
"I can't do that."

00:03:26.805 --> 00:03:29.876
So I decided to join
the Navy instead.

00:03:29.876 --> 00:03:31.444
And then I didn't join the Navy,

00:03:31.444 --> 00:03:32.945
and I became an actor, and...

00:03:32.945 --> 00:03:36.482
[ Laughter ]
And that's my life.

00:03:36.482 --> 00:03:37.850
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:40.219
Well, we're very lucky
to have a front-row seat for it.

00:03:40.219 --> 00:03:41.921
Thanks for being here, man.
-Thank you. Cheers, man.

00:03:41.921 --> 00:03:43.189
-What a pleasure.
-Thank you.

00:03:43.189 --> 00:03:46.192
-James McAvoy, everybody!
First guest of 2024!

00:03:46.192 --> 00:03:48.227
"The Book of Clarence"
is in theaters January 12th.

00:03:48.227 --> 00:03:49.762
We'll be right back
with Rachel Dratch.

